issues.body:
## Summary

On the **Fabric** loader, Village Spawn Point never disables its own spawn logic when Biome Spawn Point is also installed, even though that fallback is clearly intended (and works correctly on Forge/NeoForge). This causes the two mods to fight over `WORLD_SET_SPAWN`, producing an inconsistent/incorrect world spawn instead of the intended "village near the chosen biome" behavior.

## Root cause

`VillageSpawnEvent.onWorldLoad` is supposed to bail out entirely when Biome Spawn Point is present, deferring to it:

https://github.com/Serilum/Village-Spawn-Point/blob/321577b7470c8188ff66f5dea3ad64acab8417da/Common/src/main/java/com/natamus/villagespawnpoint/events/VillageSpawnEvent.java#L18-L21

```java
public static boolean onWorldLoad(ServerLevel serverLevel, ServerLevelData serverLevelData) {
    if (Constants.biomeSpawnPointLoaded) {
        return false;
    }
    ...
```

`Constants.biomeSpawnPointLoaded` is set correctly on Forge and NeoForge:

https://github.com/Serilum/Village-Spawn-Point/blob/321577b7470c8188ff66f5dea3ad64acab8417da/Forge/src/main/java/com/natamus/villagespawnpoint/ModForge.java#L38-L40
```java
private static void setGlobalConstants() {
    Constants.biomeSpawnPointLoaded = ModList.isLoaded("biomespawnpoint");
}
```

But on **Fabric**, the return value of `isModLoaded(...)` is discarded and never assigned:

https://github.com/Serilum/Village-Spawn-Point/blob/321577b7470c8188ff66f5dea3ad64acab8417da/Fabric/src/main/java/com/natamus/villagespawnpoint/ModFabric.java#L35-L37
```java
private static void setGlobalConstants() {
    GlobalFabricObjects.fabricLoader.isModLoaded("biomespawnpoint");
}
```

Because of this, `Constants.biomeSpawnPointLoaded` stays `false` forever on Fabric, regardless of whether Biome Spawn Point is installed. `VillageSpawnEvent` therefore keeps running and keeps calling `serverLevel.setRespawnData(...)` on the same `WORLD_SET_SPAWN` event that Biome Spawn Point also listens to:

https://github.com/Serilum/Village-Spawn-Point/blob/321577b7470c8188ff66f5dea3ad64acab8417da/Fabric/src/main/java/com/natamus/villagespawnpoint/ModFabric.java#L29-L33

Both mods end up independently setting the world spawn on the same event, and whichever handler happens to run last (order depends on mod load order, which isn't guaranteed) overwrites the other's result. This defeats Biome Spawn Point's own combined logic (finding the nearest village *near the chosen biome*) — you instead get a non-deterministic mix of "nearest village to 0,0" (from Village Spawn Point) and/or "nearest chosen biome" (from Biome Spawn Point), never the intended combination, on Fabric only.

## Fix

One-line fix, mirroring what Forge/NeoForge already do:

```java
private static void setGlobalConstants() {
    Constants.biomeSpawnPointLoaded = GlobalFabricObjects.fabricLoader.isModLoaded("biomespawnpoint");
}
```

(plus adding `import com.natamus.villagespawnpoint.data.Constants;` to `Fabric/src/main/java/com/natamus/villagespawnpoint/ModFabric.java`)

I've verified this compiles and restores the intended "Village Spawn Point defers to Biome Spawn Point when both are present" behavior on Fabric, matching the Forge/NeoForge code path. 

## Environment

- Village Spawn Point: 4.7 (source at commit `321577b`, targeting MC 26.2.0)
- Biome Spawn Point: latest (installed alongside)
- Loader: Fabric
- Also affects: any Fabric setup running both Village Spawn Point and Biome Spawn Point together

